WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:07.210
Organisms aren’t immortal.

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:08.720
They eventually die!

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.820
So who will make sure that
organisms will still exist in nature?

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:18.720
A simple and efficient system in us makes
sure that the species will be

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:23.640
perpetuated, that is continued in nature even
after we die!

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.680
I am referring to
the REPRODUCTION SYSTEM in us!

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:32.119
And not only in us, but the system in all
the animals, plants and the lower

00:00:32.119 --> 00:00:37.100
unicellular organisms is extremely important.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.850
It makes sure of the continuation
of species!

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:42.039
So where do we begin?

00:00:42.039 --> 00:00:46.960
We need to first understand the process of
reproduction.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:50.920
It is important for us
to know how exactly this process of reproduction

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:52.640
is carried out.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:56.540
So let us begin with learning about the PROCESS
OF REPRODUCTION in this

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:57.730
video.

00:00:57.730 --> 00:01:00.480
How will we define the process in simplest
words?

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:03.890
Let us divide the word itself!

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:06.200
The word “Re” means again.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.930
And production means making!

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:13.360
So can we define
the process as making something again?

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:14.630
Absolutely!

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:16.450
And what is being made
here?

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:18.720
Of course the organisms!

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:21.140
Now you may say that the new born babies are
not

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:23.299
exactly the same like parents.

00:01:23.299 --> 00:01:25.630
So how can we say “Again”?

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:29.950
Well it is not the same organism, but it is
the same species.

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:33.390
A mango tree gives rise to a mango tree.

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:36.030
While a cat gives birth to kitten!

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:38.340
So this is what we mean by Reproduction!

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:41.810
Producing the same species every
time.

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:47.579
So now the next question that pops up in our
mind is that will all the organisms

00:01:47.579 --> 00:01:49.990
reproduce in the same manner?

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:55.950
Will unicellular bacteria and huge whales
reproduce in a similar way?

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:58.079
Definitely
not!

00:01:58.079 --> 00:02:02.579
If there are several differences in the body
structures and other life processes

00:02:02.579 --> 00:02:07.929
of all organisms, then how can the reproduction
pattern be the same?

00:02:07.929 --> 00:02:12.170
This gets us the two major types of reproduction
patterns.

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:16.580
The first type is followed by the unicellular
organisms.

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:22.550
Now since it is just one single cell that
carries out all the activities, it is obvious

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:27.170
that even reproduction will be done by the
same tiny creature!

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:31.660
So this type is
the Asexual reproduction.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:35.320
In this type no specialised cells called sex
cells or

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:38.110
gametes will be produced inside the body.

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:42.430
The single cell will divide in two to
form daughter cells.

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:45.230
And it is done!

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:50.340
On the other hand in case of multi cellular
organisms, the body has specialised

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:55.590
cells called gametes which fuse to form the
new individual.

00:02:55.590 --> 00:03:00.100
Such type is
referred to as Sexual Reproduction.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:04.290
We will learn about the first type that is
Asexual Reproduction in the

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:05.090
upcoming video.

